1. 飲茶  
廣東話：我哋聽日朝早去飲茶，順便傾吓生意。  
English: We are going to yum cha tomorrow morning and talk business while we're at it.

2. 圖書館  
廣東話：呢間圖書館開到夜晚十點，好方便學生溫書。  
English: This library is open until 10 p.m., which is very convenient for students to study.

3. 養聲  
廣東話：歌手開演唱會之前一定要養聲，唔可以亂咁嗌。  
English: Singers must rest their voice before a concert and must not shout randomly.

4. 票尾  
廣東話：記得留返張票尾，入場嗰陣要核對。  
English: Remember to keep the ticket stub, as it will be checked when you enter.

5. hacker  
廣東話：嗰個黑客入侵咗公司嘅系統，偷走咗好多機密資料。  
English: That hacker broke into the company's system and stole a lot of confidential data.

6. 石斛蘭  
廣東話：石斛蘭鍾意依附喺樹幹上面生長，好靚㗎。  
English: Dendrobium orchids like to grow on tree trunks and look very beautiful.

7. 吊詭（矛盾、悖論）  
廣東話：呢個情況真係好吊詭，明明話開放，但係又限制多多。  
English: This situation is really paradoxical—it claims to be open, yet there are many restrictions.

8. 吊詭（似非而是、荒謬）  
廣東話：佢講嘅嘢好吊詭，聽落好似合理，但其實講唔通。  
English: What he said sounds plausible but is actually absurd—it's quite paradoxical.

9. 各為其主  
廣東話：兩隊球員各為其主，喺場上梗係要盡力爭勝。  
English: The players on both teams are each serving their own side, so of course they fight hard to win.

10. 軨蓋  
廣東話：我架車嘅軨蓋甩咗一個，要買返個新嘅裝返。  
English: One of my wheel covers fell off, so I need to buy a new one to put back on.

11. 打哥夫  
廣東話：佢每逢週末都會去會所打哥夫，鬆一鬆。  
English: He goes to the club to play golf every weekend to relax.

12. 免揀  
廣東話：呢檔生果係免揀嘅，你唔可以自己揀，老闆話點就點。  
English: This fruit stall is no-choice—you can't pick your own; whatever the boss gives you is final.

13. 擺闊佬  
廣東話：佢成日喺朋友面前擺闊佬，其實欠落周身債。  
English: He always shows off his wealth in front of friends, but in reality he's deep in debt.

14. 廣播劇  
廣東話：細個嗰陣好鍾意聽電台嘅廣播劇，覺得好有畫面。  
English: When I was little, I loved listening to radio dramas—they felt so vivid.

15. 錄影機  
廣東話：以前屋企有部錄影機，成日錄低啲電視節目嚟睇。  
English: We used to have a video recorder at home and would often record TV shows to watch.

16. 吟詩吟唔甩  
廣東話：佢偷食嘅證據擺喺度，今次吟詩吟唔甩喇。  
English: The evidence of his cheating is right here—this time he can't talk his way out of it.

17. 佈道大會  
廣東話：教會下個月會舉辦一場大型佈道大會，歡迎各界人士參加。  
English: The church will hold a large evangelistic rally next month, and everyone is welcome.

18. 寫手（寫作嘅人）  
廣東話：呢位寫手嘅文章好有深度，好多讀者都追住睇。  
English: This writer's articles are very insightful, and many readers follow them closely.

19. 寫手（代替他人寫作嘅人）  
廣東話：佢係一位代筆寫手，幫明星寫自傳。  
English: He is a ghostwriter who writes autobiographies for celebrities.

20. 代打  
廣東話：我今晚冇時間上線，你可唔可以幫我代打一場？  
English: I don't have time to go online tonight—can you play a match for me?

21. 茶碗  
廣東話：呢隻茶碗係日本師傅手造嘅，好有質感。  
English: This tea bowl is handmade by a Japanese craftsman and has a lovely texture.

22. 茶隔  
廣東話：沖茶嗰陣記得用茶隔，咁就唔會飲到茶葉。  
English: Remember to use a tea strainer when brewing tea, so you won't get tea leaves in your cup.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈  
廣東話：老闆自己遲到就冇事，我哋遲到就扣錢，真係只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈。  
English: The boss can be late without any issue, but if we're late we get fined—it's really a case of "one rule for the rich, another for the poor."

24. 獨唱  
廣東話：今晚佢會喺音樂會上獨唱一首經典金曲。  
English: Tonight she will perform a classic song as a solo at the concert.

25. 快人快事  
廣東話：佢做事一向快人快事，話做就做，唔會拖泥帶水。  
English: He's always quick and decisive—when he says he'll do something, he just does it without hesitation.

26. 四腳獸  
廣東話：聽講嗰個公廁成日有「四腳獸」，夜晚都冇人敢去。  
English: I heard that public toilet often has "four-legged beasts" at night, so no one dares to go there.

27. 無米粥  
廣東話：呢單生意而家仲係煲無米粥，未傾到實際條件。  
English: This deal is still just preliminary talk—we haven't gotten down to the actual terms yet.

28. 義會  
廣東話：以前啲人冇錢周轉，就會參加義會，大家夾錢輪流用。  
English: In the old days, people without money would join a rotating credit association, pooling funds and taking turns to use them.

29. 榜文  
廣東話：城門口貼咗一張榜文，話要捉拿通緝犯。  
English: A notice was posted at the city gate saying they were looking for a wanted criminal.

30. MK名  
廣東話：佢個MK名改到好搞笑，叫「醉愛·小霸王」。  
English: His MK-style username is hilarious—it's "Drunk Love · Little Tyrant." [end of text]


